<title>INDIA: India's Siemens 1996/97 1st half loss.</title>
<headline>India's Siemens 1996/97 1st half loss.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     (239.0)   vs    224.0</p>
<p>    Net sales	     6,630.0    vs  5,330.0</p>
<p>    Interest		  481.0    vs    204.5</p>
<p>    Gross profit	     28.0    vs    534.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    267.0    vs    175.0</p>
<p>    Tax			   nil    vs    135.0</p>
<p>Note: Siemens India Ltd said the continued encouraging performance of its core divisions had been overshadowed by the considerable losses experienced by the telecommunication division. This was due to &quot;delays in ordering by the Department of Telecommunication and slow progress as regards to basic services investment by private operators&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company said &quot;as a result of the ongoing unsatisfactory situation of its telecommunication business, Siemens has decided to restructure this operation.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Barring unforeseen circumstances, the restructuring of the company is expected to yield positive results hopefully in the course of the next six months.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
